exercices:

* Define an unless macro without depending on Kernel.if, by using other con-
  structs in Elixir for control flow.
* Define a macro that returns a raw AST that you’ve written by hand, instead
  of using quote for code generation.

<!-- livebook:{"break_markdown":true} -->

Exercice 1

```elixir
# my solution
defmodule ExerciseOne do
  defmacro customUnless(expr, do: block) do
    quote do
      case unquote(expr) do
        true -> nil
        false -> unquote(block)
      end
    end
  end
end
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
{:module, ExerciseOne, <<70, 79, 82, 49, 0, 0, 7, ...>>, ...}
```

```elixir
require ExerciseOne
ExerciseOne.customUnless 5 == 4 do
  "Hello"
end
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
"Hello"
```

